# Named `.dockerignore` rather than `.containerignore` because Podman reads both
# and Docker reads only this one (AD-022: one file, two runtimes).
#
# The Containerfile copies explicit paths rather than the tree, so this is a
# second line of defence rather than the primary one. It matters most for `.env`
# and `data/`: a build context that carries a secret has already leaked it to the
# daemon, whatever the Containerfile then chooses to COPY.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
data/
*.spill.jsonl

.git/
.github/
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/

.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

**/tests/
apps/kb-api/bruno/
ai-kb/
docs/
graphify-out/
compose*.yml
justfile
*.md
